nical specification (all ten protocols)"}]}],"id":"blk-74400","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107572","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-008-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-107573","text":" — the Agent Harness Protocol specification"}]}],"id":"blk-74402","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107574","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-107575","text":" — PRISM diagnostic benchmark protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-74404","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107576","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-107577","text":" — PULSE loop manifest standard"}]}],"id":"blk-74406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107578","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION"},{"id":"spn-107579","text":" — empirical evaluation of topology-aware continual learning"}]}],"id":"blk-74408","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74410","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107580","text":"Documentation index"}]},{"id":"blk-74411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107581","text":"Linked index of every page in this set (renders on GitHub and in the docs atlas; the toctrees above drive the Sphinx build):"}]},{"id":"blk-74412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107582","marks":["bold"],"text":"Guides"}]},{"id":"blk-74413","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107583","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"Quickstart"}]}],"id":"blk-74414","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107584","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/runtime-walkthrough.md"}],"text":"Runtime Walkthrough"}]}],"id":"blk-74416","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107585","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/positioning.md"}],"text":"Positioning — The Missing Constraint: Runtime Governance in the Agent Stack"}]}],"id":"blk-74418","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107586","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/competitive-landscape.md"}],"text":"Competitive Landscape — Agent Governance and Runtime Enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-74420","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107587","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/comparison-table.md"}],"text":"Comparison — OpenSentience vs. Alternatives"}]}],"id":"blk-74422","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107588","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ecosystem-overview.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem Overview — How the Protocols Connect"}]}],"id":"blk-74424","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107589","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/research.md"}],"text":"Research Overview"}]}],"id":"blk-74426","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74429","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107590","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/faq.md"}],"text":"FAQ"}]}],"id":"blk-74428","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74431","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107591","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/skills/SKILLS.md"}],"text":"Agent Skills"}]}],"id":"blk-74430","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107592","marks":["bold"],"text":"Specifications"}]},{"id":"blk-74433","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74435","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107593","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"OS-011 — Embodiment Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-74434","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107594","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"OS-E001 — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning"}]}],"id":"blk-74436","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107595","marks":["bold"],"text":"UX & build prompts"}]},{"id":"blk-74439","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107596","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ux/user-stories-embodiment.md"}],"text":"Embodiment (body-browser + body-os) — User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-74440","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107597","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/prompts/OS-008-BUILD.md"}],"text":"OS-008 Agent Harness Protocol — Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-74442","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74444","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107598","text":"The Three Enforcement Layers"}]},{"id":"blk-74445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107599","text":"OpenSentience provides three layers of runtime enforcement:"}]},{"id":"blk-74446","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OS-008 Harness:   \"Has this agent followed the correct process?\"\n                   Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts\n\nOS-006 Shim:      \"Is this agent allowed to do this?\"\n                   Permissions, lifecycle, autonomy levels\n\nOS-007 Security:  \"Is this agent under attack?\"\n                   Threat detection, identity verification, circuit breakers"},{"id":"blk-74447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107600","text":"All three log to the same append-only audit trail, creating a unified compliance record from protocol to permission to pipeline."}]},{"id":"blk-74448","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107601","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-74449","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107602","text":"Above the cognitive primitives, OpenSentience publishes three sibling protocols that together turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate:"}]},{"id":"blk-74450","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009) — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010) — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&] Protocol     — composes capabilities     structural│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-74452","spans":[{"id":"spn-107603","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-74453","spans":[{"id":"spn-107604","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-74454","spans":[{"id":"spn-107605","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-74451","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-74455","spans":[{"id":"spn-107606","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-74456","spans":[{"id":"spn-107607","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-74457","spans":[{"id":"spn-107608","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-74458","spans":[{"id":"spn-107609","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-74459","spans":[{"id":"spn-107610","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-74460","spans":[{"id":"spn-107611","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-107612","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-74461","spans":[{"id":"spn-107613","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-74462","spans":[{"id":"spn-107614","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-74463","spans":[{"id":"spn-107615","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-74464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107616","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-107617","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-107618","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-107619","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-107620","text":" and its runtime passes the 12-test conformance suite. A system is "},{"id":"spn-107621","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-107622","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-107623","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-107624","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-107625","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-107626","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-107627","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-107628","text":" phase. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-74465","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107629","text":"Relationship to the [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-74466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107630","text":"OpenSentience occupies the "},{"id":"spn-107631","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance and research layer"},{"id":"spn-107632","text":" of the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-74467","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  [&] Protocol        — capability composition (what an agent CAN do)\n  OpenSentience       — governance + harness (what an agent MAY do, and how)\n  Graphonomous        — memory + learning (OS-001, OS-002, OS-004, OS-005)\n  AgenTroMatic        — deliberation (OS-003)\n  Delegatic           — policy authoring (feeds into OS-006 enforcement)\n  Agentelic           — agent manifests (consumed by OS-006 install)\n  FleetPrompt         — marketplace (agents enter governance on install)\n  SpecPrompt          — acceptance criteria (consumed by OS-008 quality gates)"},{"id":"blk-74468","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107633","text":"The governance shim wraps any OTP "},{"id":"spn-107634","marks":["code"],"text":"child_spec"},{"id":"spn-107635","text":". It does not replace the supervised process — it interposes permission checks, lifecycle management, autonomy control, pipeline enforcement, and audit logging around it."}]},{"id":"blk-74469","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107636","text":"Founding Thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-74470","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107637","text":"OpenSentience exists because intelligence without governance is generation without accumulation. The ten protocols formalize what structured accumulation requires: memory that consolidates, routing that detects cycles, deliberation that resolves conflict, attention that prioritizes, resources that adapt, governance that enforces boundaries, security that detects threats, a harness that orchestrates the entire pipeline, "},{"id":"spn-107638","marks":["bold"],"text":"diagnostics that measure whether the loop actually learns"},{"id":"spn-107639","text":" (PRISM), and a "},{"id":"spn-107640","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal manifest"},{"id":"spn-107641","text":" that lets every loop in the ecosystem declare how it cycles and signals (PULSE)."}]},{"id":"blk-74471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107642","text":"The shim is deliberately thin. Governance should cost less than 1% of the system it governs. PULSE is a manifest standard with no required runtime. PRISM runs as a separate benchmark engine that any system can opt into via its PULSE manifest."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierav53rkyv6b2ihpyaj4osheavdngj5lxev5gihrfmeqwbbftzmunha","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}